WEBVTT

00:13:28.488 --> 00:13:31.345
I spent nine months
as a participant observer in a firm,

00:13:31.369 --> 00:13:33.194
watching the recruiting process.

00:13:33.218 --> 00:13:34.408
AG: At one bank,

00:13:34.432 --> 00:13:37.178
she asked leaders if they knew
what predicts performance.

00:13:37.202 --> 00:13:38.885
LR: They said, "Fuckin' lacrosse."

00:13:38.909 --> 00:13:40.458
I was like, "What do you mean?"

00:13:40.482 --> 00:13:42.498
They said, "All the MDs
here play lacrosse,

00:13:42.522 --> 00:13:44.584
so that's why we look
for a lacrosse player.

00:13:44.608 --> 00:13:45.783
He'll do awesome here."

00:13:45.807 --> 00:13:48.713
I was like, "Do you ever hire people
who don't play lacrosse?"

00:13:48.737 --> 00:13:49.898
They said, "No."

00:13:49.942 --> 00:13:52.897
AG: Interviewers were convinced
that playing sports was a proxy

00:13:52.921 --> 00:13:54.341
for grit and teamwork skills.

00:13:54.365 --> 00:13:56.048
But there are many other activities

00:13:56.072 --> 00:13:58.303
that can build those
character strengths, too.

00:13:58.327 --> 00:14:00.740
Surprisingly, many interviewers
were less concerned